&lt;h1&gt;📘 Topic: Cipher Feedback (CFB) Mode&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; D6 – Security Engineering&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #cissp&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🧾 Definition&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-definition&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-definition&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cipher Feedback Mode is a block cipher mode of operation that turns a block cipher into a self-synchronizing stream-like mechanism. It uses previous ciphertext to produce the next keystream block.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔑 Key Points&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-points&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-points&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CFB is a block cipher mode used for encryption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It can operate like a stream cipher and is useful for real-time data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It propagates errors from earlier ciphertext blocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It is a legacy mode; modern systems usually prefer AEAD modes such as GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚠️ CISSP Insight&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-cissp-insight&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-cissp-insight&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP candidates should understand that encryption mode choice affects security properties, performance, and error behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern design should prefer authenticated encryption over legacy modes where possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚔️ Key Difference / Trap&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-difference--trap&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-difference--trap&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CFB vs ECB&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ECB encrypts identical plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CFB avoids that pattern by chaining previous ciphertext&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CFB vs CTR&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CFB is feedback-based&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CTR uses a counter value for keystream generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🏗️ Example&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-example&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-example&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;CFB may be used in legacy protocols where a block cipher is required in a stream-like fashion, but modern implementations usually prefer authenticated encryption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;📚 References&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-references&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-references&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NIST SP 800-38A, Recommendation for Block Cipher Modes of Operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NIST SP 800-57, Recommendation for Key Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔁 Quick Recall&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-quick-recall&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-quick-recall&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CFB = Feedback-based block cipher mode&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern choice = AEAD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>[13] RFC 1918 Private Address Space</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d6/13-rfc-1918/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d6/13-rfc-1918/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280; display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px;&#34;&gt;
  
    &lt;span style=&#34;display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;&#34;&gt;
      By:
      
        
        
        
        
          
          
          
            
          
          
          &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/prasannavbalaji&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34; style=&#34;display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-weight: 600; color: #0a66c2; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;&#34; onmouseover=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid #0a66c2&#39;&#34; onmouseout=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid transparent&#39;&#34;&gt;
